      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a regression test that fails the build if any module under\n`src/llamafactory/webui` hardcodes `trust_remote_code=True` again, plus a check that the\nnew `LLAMAFACTORY_WEBUI_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE` opt-in defaults to **off**.\n\nCompanion to the main fix in #10903.\n\n## Finding\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** | Unauthenticated remote code execution in the Gradio WebUI via `trust_remote_code=True` on an attacker-controlled model path |\n| **Severity** | CRITICAL |\n| **CVSS** | 9.8 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) |\n| **Scan ID** | `cmvgxjs4n00kzqn01fnzaqwf5` |\n\n## PoC summary\n\nAn unauthenticated POST to the Gradio queue join endpoint for the Load-model handler with\n`model_path` pointing at an attacker-controlled HF-style repo made `transformers` import and\nexecute the repo's `configuration_evil.py` inside the server process (marker written on host) —\nbefore any weights load.\n\n## What this test does\n\n- `test_webui_does_not_hardcode_trust_remote_code` — parametrized over every `*.py` under\n  `src/llamafactory/webui`, asserts no literal `trust_remote_code=True` argument exists.\n- `test_webui_remote_code_gate_defaults_to_disabled` — asserts\n  `is_env_enabled(\"LLAMAFACTORY_WEBUI_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE\")` is `False` when the env var is unset.\n\nRun with:\n\n```bash\npytest tests/webui/test_no_hardcoded_trust_remote_code.py\n```\n\n## Fix explanation\n\nThis test *enforces* the fix from #10903: remote code execution is only reachable through an\nexplicit server-side opt-in, never through a user-supplied model path. Any future change that\nreintroduces a hardcoded `True` will fail CI.\n\n---\nAutomated security test by [FailSafe Security](https://getfailsafe.com) — scan `cmvgxjs4n00kzqn01fnzaqwf5`.\n",
